This scaffold instantiates the SRA OU shape and the seven landing-zone
foundational features. Operators take this scaffold to AWS Control Tower (or
Landing Zone Accelerator if Control Tower is not viable) to provision.

---

## SRA-aligned OU + account layout

```
Org root ({{landing_zone_name}})
├── (Org Management account)              <- billing, SCPs, AWS Organizations
├── Security OU
│   ├── Security Tooling account          <- delegated admin: GuardDuty, SecHub, Inspector, Macie, Access Analyzer
│   └── Log Archive account               <- Org CloudTrail S3 + KMS, immutable
├── Infrastructure OU
│   ├── Network account                   <- TGW, central egress, NFW, DNS
│   └── Shared Services account           <- IAM Identity Center, image factory, internal mirrors
└── Workloads OU
    └── workloads/<app>-<env>/            <- one account per (app x env)
```

Workload accounts inherit SCPs from the Workloads OU (deny: leave-org,
disable-cloudtrail, root-actions, public-S3 by default, IMDSv1, …).

## Seven landing-zone foundational features (compliance checklist)

| # | Feature | Where it's addressed |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Multi-account architecture | The OU/account layout above; Control Tower account factory or LZA. |
| 2 | Initial security baseline | Security Tooling: GuardDuty, Security Hub (CIS + AWS Foundational + PCI), Inspector, Macie, Access Analyzer; Config rules; Org-trail. |
| 3 | Identity and access management | IAM Identity Center in Shared Services; permission sets per persona; no IAM users; OIDC for CI. |
| 4 | Governance | SCPs on each OU; Control Tower guardrails (or LZA equivalents); Config conformance packs; tag policies. |
| 5 | Data security | KMS CMKs per account; S3 default encryption; AWS Backup vaults with delete-protection; PrivateLink for in-account services. |
| 6 | Network design | Single TGW in the Network account; non-overlapping VPC CIDRs; centralised egress via NFW; centralised inbound resolvers. |
| 7 | Logging | Org CloudTrail to Log Archive S3 with bucket policy denying writes outside org; CloudWatch cross-account observability sink in Security Tooling. |

## Per-account responsibilities

### Org Management account

- AWS Organizations management; OUs; SCPs.
- Consolidated billing; AWS Cost Explorer; AWS Cost Categories.
- IAM Identity Center delegated admin handoff to Shared Services.
- **Hard rule**: no workload runs here. No human signs in here except for
  break-glass.

### Security Tooling account (Security OU)

- Delegated admin for: GuardDuty, Security Hub, Inspector, Macie, IAM Access
  Analyzer, Detective, Audit Manager.
- AWS Config aggregator (org-wide).
- CloudWatch cross-account observability sink (read).
- Security findings -> EventBridge -> SNS -> Catalyst `webhook-handler` ->
  GitHub Issue with `type/ops-intel-finding` per ADR-001.

### Log Archive account (Security OU)

- Centralised S3 buckets for: Org CloudTrail, S3 access logs, VPC flow logs,
  Config snapshots/history, ALB access logs.
- Bucket policies deny `s3:DeleteObject` and `s3:PutBucketPolicy` to anyone
  except the organization.
- KMS CMK with key policy denying decrypt to anyone outside Security Tooling
  + Org Management.
- Lifecycle rules: hot 30d -> IA 90d -> Glacier IT 365d -> deep archive 7y.

### Network account (Infrastructure OU)

- AWS Transit Gateway (regional pair across primary + DR).
- Centralised egress VPC with AWS Network Firewall.
- Centralised inbound resolvers (Route 53 Resolver endpoints).
- Direct Connect / Site-to-Site VPN (if hybrid).
- IPAM pools for workload VPCs (no overlapping CIDRs).

### Shared Services account (Infrastructure OU)

- IAM Identity Center (SSO).
- Golden AMI factory (EC2 Image Builder).
- Internal package mirrors (CodeArtifact / ECR pull-through cache).
- Centralised AppConfig / Parameter Store for shared config.

### Workload accounts (Workloads OU) — one per (app x env)

- Application runtime (ECS / EKS / Lambda) per the
  `generate-platform-service-skeleton` capability.
- Per-account KMS CMK; per-account secrets in Secrets Manager.
- VPC attached to the regional TGW; routes to centralised egress.
- IAM roles assumed via IAM Identity Center permission sets and OIDC for CI.

## Mapping to Catalyst's construct hierarchy (ADR-002)

| Construct level | AWS primitive |
|---|---|
| Tenant | AWS Org root |
| Environment-class | OU (Workloads OU subdivides into env-class sub-OUs if scale demands it) |
| Landing Zone | Account |
| Project / Application | Tags + IAM scoping within the workload account |

